# Kafka operations safety

Source of truth: `docs/adr/0008-operations-engine.md` and `docs/adr/0007-dynamic-quorum.md`.

- Every mutating operation has a dry run that returns the plan without side effects.
- Before each step run the health gate: no offline partitions, no under-replicated partitions
  except those in the current reassignment, nothing under `min.insync.replicas`, quorum has a
  leader, voters caught up, no other running operation on the cluster.
- Reassignments: full target replica lists, `allowReplicationFactorChange=false` semantics,
  batches, broker and topic throttles set before and removed after (also on failure or cancel).
- Never move or keep a replica on a cordoned or draining broker; check free disk on targets.
- Quorum: one voter change at a time; add the new voter after it caught up as an observer, then
  remove the old one. Never remove the last voter. Brokerium does not enable controller auto-join.
- After unregistering a broker, delete its `cordoned.log.dirs` config so a future broker with the
  same id is not cordoned.
- Irreversible actions (`metadata.version` / `kraft.version` finalization, unregister, wipe) need
  an explicit confirmation carrying the cluster name.
- Storage is formatted with the same Kafka version that will run the node (KIP-1170 in 4.4).
